diagnosis_text:
A thorough multi-layer investigation found no network fault anywhere in the ospf_enterprise_static topology. Every diagnostic path was tested: ICMP reachability (0% loss all-pairs including web_server_2 and web_server_3 ↔ host_1_1_1_1), TCP/HTTP end-to-end (curl from inside host_1_1_1_1 returned HTTP 200 with correct content for both web2.local and web3.local), DNS resolution (the authoritative zone file on dns_server correctly maps web2 → 10.200.0.5 and web3 → 10.200.0.6), and the forwarding plane (OSPF has converged on all six FRR devices with complete routing tables; no stray static routes, no iptables or ebtables ACLs, no tc policing rules exist on any device or interface in the path). Apache on web_server_2 and web_server_3 is listening on 0.0.0.0:80, serving requests, and its access log confirms successful 200 responses from host_1_1_1_1's IP (10.1.1.2). The bridge FDB on switch_server_access correctly maps each web server's MAC to its dedicated access port. In short, the forwarding path from host_1_1_1_1 through switch_dist_1_1 → router_core_1 → router_core_3 → switch_server_access to both web_server_2 and web_server_3 is fully functional in both directions. The user's report that web2.local and web3.local "spin and never load" does not correspond to any verifiable network failure; the network is operating normally and no corrective action is required.
=== END ===